# Difference btw null and undefined:
- `null` is an assignment value that represents the intentional absence of any object value.
-(`Explicitely` set by the programmer to indicate that a variable should have no value.)
- `undefined` is a variable that has been declared but has not been assigned a value.
(`Implicitly` set by JavaScript when a variable is declared by not assigned a value, or when a function does not return a value.)

